{\b Try ArrowKeys}
\par ArrowKeys opens automatically for the signed-in user. Open {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_Accessibility"}{\fldrslt\ul Accessibility Settings}}, then turn on {\b ArrowKeys}. If prompted, choose {\b Quit & Reopen}. Only you can give the app permission to move the cursor in other apps.
\par Already on after an update? Select the old ArrowKeys entry and click the minus button. Click + to add ArrowKeys from Applications again, then turn it on.
\par Open the four-arrow menu. When it shows {\b Navigation active}, try Caps Lock + J in a text editor to move the cursor left.
\par Open at Login is on by default. You can turn it off in the ArrowKeys menu. If upgrading from the Karabiner edition, remove its ArrowKeys rule in Complex Modifications.
\par To uninstall, move ArrowKeys.app from Applications to Trash. Quitting ArrowKeys or moving the running app to Trash restores the previous Caps Lock assignment on each keyboard it changed.
}
